# Seeing the API work, without leaving VS Code.
#
# Install the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client), then click the
# "Send Request" link that appears above each ### block below.
#
# Run `npm run dev` first. Log in before the requests that need a token —
# REST Client reuses the login response, so the Authorization headers below
# fill themselves in.

@host = http://localhost:3000

###
# Is the server up? This one also works in a browser.
GET {{host}}/health

###
# @name login
# A teacher at the seeded demo school.
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantSlug": "demo-school",
  "email": "teacher@demo-school.test",
  "password": "demo-password-123"
}

###
# Who am I, and what am I allowed to do?
# Note `permissions` — resolved from the role matrix on every request,
# never carried in the token.
GET {{host}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

###
# This school's students. Empty until you create one below.
GET {{host}}/students
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

###
# A teacher may READ students but not create them: expect 403 with
# "This action requires the student:manage permission".
POST {{host}}/students
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Should Be Rejected",
  "classLabel": "10-A"
}

###
# @name adminLogin
# The same school's admin, who does have student:manage.
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantSlug": "demo-school",
  "email": "admin@demo-school.test",
  "password": "demo-password-123"
}

###
# Expect 201 and the created student.
POST {{host}}/students
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Priya Sharma",
  "classLabel": "10-A"
}

###
# Now the list has her in it.
GET {{host}}/students
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

###
# A parent sees a narrower permission set: result:read and fee:read,
# but no student:manage.
# @name parentLogin
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantSlug": "demo-school",
  "email": "parent@demo-school.test",
  "password": "demo-password-123"
}

###
GET {{host}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{parentLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

###
# Wrong password: 401, and the body is identical to what an unknown
# email or an unknown school returns. That is deliberate — the endpoint
# will not tell you which accounts exist.
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantSlug": "demo-school",
  "email": "teacher@demo-school.test",
  "password": "definitely-the-wrong-password"
}
